findings.finding:
The acceptance criteria cover only service-user.sh, the AGENTS.md/CONTRIBUTING.md examples and the guard. They do not cover several deliverables:
- the new `lib-credentials.sh` helpers actually authenticating (curl_auth Basic header, git_auth urlmatch scoping to the Gerrit host only);
- the five converted e2e/smoke/inventory scripts still working;
- the workflow Jira cleanup;
- the four additional runbooks/docs.
AC3 ('covers these files and passes') proves only the absence of argv patterns. A script that no longer authenticates, or a git_auth header that leaks to github.com, would still satisfy every AC.
